1:["$","$Ld",null,{"item":{"id":"title-the-finding","number":"06","title":"Put the finding in the title.","mode":"Buried takeaway","scale":"slide","dek":"Use a results slide’s title to state the finding the audience should remember. Match the strength of that statement to what the evidence supports.","before":[{"kind":"image","title":"Baseline Results · PDF p. 39","image":"/originals/elite-p39.png","alt":"Baseline Results: aid coefficients 3.391, −1.511, and 4.973 for haven deposits, non-haven deposits, and their ratio. Full table includes standard errors, GDP-growth controls, fixed effects, observations, and R-squared.","id":"aid-table","sourcePage":"39","provenance":"Original slide · Haven and non-haven columns report growth in foreign bank deposits."}],"after":[{"kind":"aid-results","title":"Aid disbursements coincide with rising haven deposits.","alt":"Rebuilt regression table. All coefficients, standard errors, significance marks, controls, observation counts, and R-squared values are retained.","revises":["aid-table"]}],"diagnosis":"A topic title leaves the audience to extract the finding from the table. Naming the observed relationship gives every number a question to answer.","changes":["Replace the topic label with a proportionate finding.","Keep the full table, including the non-haven result.","Use “coincide” to describe the reported relationship."],"preserved":"All six coefficients and standard errors, source significance marks, fixed effects, observation counts, R-squared values, and country clustering.","deferred":"Interpretation and alternative explanations remain in the surrounding talk. The revised title makes no claim that the table alone proves theft.","practice":"Read your slide titles aloud without their bodies. Do they say what your audience should remember?","principle":"Takeaways before details","sourceType":"public","context":"The authors preview the main findings on PDF pp. 11–12. This is a local title revision to p. 39; p. 40 already uses a substantive title.","beforeCaption":"","afterCaption":"","values":["Aid (% GDP): haven 3.391 (1.154); non-haven −1.511 (1.035); ratio 4.973 (1.715).","GDP (% growth): haven 0.122 (0.141); non-haven 0.147 (0.063); ratio −0.001 (0.150).","All columns include country and time fixed effects. Standard errors clustered by country.","Observations: 1,648 / 1,652 / 1,645. R-squared: 0.101 / 0.092 / 0.076.","The dependent variable is quarterly growth in log deposits. A one-percentage-point increase in aid/GDP is associated with 3.391 log-percentage-points higher haven-deposit growth, controlling for GDP growth and country and time fixed effects."],"source":{"authors":"Jørgen Juel Andersen, Niels Johannesen, Bob Rijkers","title":"Elite Capture of Foreign Aid: Evidence from Offshore Bank Accounts","date":"2020","url":"https://thedocs.worldbank.org/en/doc/605901583339487690-0050022020/render/EliteCaptureofForeignAid.pdf","pages":"39"},"topic":"Development finance","point":"A results slide is easier to follow when listeners know which conclusion its evidence is meant to support. State that conclusion in a sentence at the top, then use the table or figure to substantiate it. Keep the wording precise about the population, comparison, and strength of inference, including whether the evidence establishes an association or a causal effect."}}]
